WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.579 --> 00:00:02.996
- [Charles] Now where is my--

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.400
- Pardon?

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.956
- Oh, that was taken over in France.

00:00:10.956 --> 00:00:14.873
And these are two of my
buddies, and that's me.

00:00:16.705 --> 00:00:17.538
Watch it.

00:00:20.823 --> 00:00:22.556
Memories are still there.

00:00:22.556 --> 00:00:24.223
I live it, I see it.

00:00:25.169 --> 00:00:29.281
I was not just a veteran, I was
in the Invasion of Normandy,

00:00:29.281 --> 00:00:31.248
in the Invasion of Normandy.

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:35.415
No one knows what war is unless
you have been there in it.

00:00:42.448 --> 00:00:44.133
- I was up late one night on my computer,

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.321
and I saw this wonderful story about

00:00:46.321 --> 00:00:48.220
Charles Adderley, a true American hero.

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.948
The people in this
community really wanna help

00:00:49.948 --> 00:00:51.811
those in need, especially
those who have given

00:00:51.811 --> 00:00:53.283
so much time serving their country

00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:55.506
and serving their
community like Charles has.

00:00:55.506 --> 00:00:57.323
He was in need of a new A/C system,

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.360
there were some mold issues, and so we all

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.527
just wanted to do everything
we could to help Charles.

00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:05.959
- Alright, Mr. Adderley.

00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:10.188
So, this was done this morning by the team.

00:01:10.188 --> 00:01:13.260
We got the drywall all patched up.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.468
So, once the flooring's done
we can start bringing in

00:01:15.468 --> 00:01:18.721
the cabinets and the
actual kitchen materials.

00:01:18.721 --> 00:01:19.948
- Sounds good to me.

00:01:19.948 --> 00:01:22.977
- Alright. (laughs)

00:01:22.977 --> 00:01:24.780
- Mr. Adderley.

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.127
When I looked at him, I
just started thinking about

00:01:27.127 --> 00:01:31.789
the possibilities of what it
was like, what he went through.

00:01:31.789 --> 00:01:35.956
And once he started talking
I snapped back and listened.

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:40.396
- Try to move me.

00:01:40.396 --> 00:01:42.669
(laughs)

00:01:42.669 --> 00:01:46.744
- You'll have a fight on your hand, yeah.

00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:47.597
- [Travis] These guys came out here,

00:01:47.597 --> 00:01:49.368
donated their time, they're professionals.

00:01:49.368 --> 00:01:50.850
All of our volunteers
and all of our partners,

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.450
everyone has just fallen
in love with Charles

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:54.692
and they wanna do
whatever they can for him.

00:01:54.692 --> 00:01:55.525
- People need help.

00:01:55.525 --> 00:01:56.981
You know, it could be you one day.

00:01:56.981 --> 00:02:00.490
You got businesses willing
to give up material.

00:02:00.490 --> 00:02:02.538
You got the firemen, we come off duty.

00:02:02.538 --> 00:02:04.737
We wanna come and put the work in.

00:02:04.737 --> 00:02:05.953
- One of the issues I see these days,

00:02:05.953 --> 00:02:07.916
especially with people
my age, is you don't

00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:09.985
interact with people who are your elders.

00:02:09.985 --> 00:02:10.945
And I mean, there's so much that

00:02:10.945 --> 00:02:12.390
can be learned from them.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.729
I spoke with Charles several times

00:02:13.729 --> 00:02:15.062
about the history of Miami.

00:02:15.062 --> 00:02:16.408
He is 93 years old.

00:02:16.408 --> 00:02:18.072
He provides that glimpse into the past,

00:02:18.072 --> 00:02:20.155
and it's just invaluable.

00:02:21.197 --> 00:02:22.947
- See the date there?

00:02:29.078 --> 00:02:31.828
- What is the definition of hero?

00:02:34.124 --> 00:02:35.174
What is it?

00:02:35.174 --> 00:02:38.342
You can see all the pictures
in the movie--well that's it,

00:02:38.342 --> 00:02:40.616
you're going about your
business you forget.

00:02:40.616 --> 00:02:42.033
I've seen it all.

00:02:43.636 --> 00:02:44.469
- You ready?

00:02:44.469 --> 00:02:47.712
- For him to enlist in the
service and fight for a country

00:02:47.712 --> 00:02:51.050
that really didn't at that time, you know,

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:55.388
favor people like he
and I, that says to me

00:02:55.388 --> 00:02:57.958
something about an individual.

00:02:57.958 --> 00:03:00.128
He inspires so many people
from different walks

00:03:00.128 --> 00:03:01.890
to wanna help him because, you know what,

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.704
quite frankly, we owe him.

00:03:03.704 --> 00:03:05.645
That's how I see it, we owe him.

00:03:05.645 --> 00:03:07.032
Somebody like that we have to always

00:03:07.032 --> 00:03:08.866
show our gratitude and appreciation.

00:03:08.866 --> 00:03:09.773
We can never let that go.

00:03:09.773 --> 00:03:12.260
And it's not just one day in November.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.677
- You've got to live in the here and now.

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:17.849
The only reason why we're in this world

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:19.545
is what we're doing right now.

00:03:19.545 --> 00:03:21.220
To be there for each other.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.204
That's what I learned from him.

00:03:23.204 --> 00:03:25.902
- I am concerned about the moment,

00:03:25.902 --> 00:03:28.601
and I know better than
to think about tomorrow.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.820
Oh my god, I can't even handle today.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:32.903
(laughs)

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:39.316
Each and every one of you
has become a part of my life.

00:03:39.316 --> 00:03:43.392
Each and every one of
you is a part of me now.

00:03:43.392 --> 00:03:44.892
That's how I feel.

00:03:46.037 --> 00:03:50.120
All I can say is thank
each and every one of you.

